## Context

Ticket 0557 (merged PR #1020) demoted positive prose-literal adherence
assertions to negative guards + `docs/editorial-brief.md`, and adopted
the CI test polarity rule (`.claude/rules/writing.md`): prose tests pin
only negative guards, mechanical checks, and loose structural anchors
(fixed *external* vocabulary, never authorial phrasing). The 0557 scope
covered `test_manuscript_cohort_and_caveats.py` only. A post-merge roar
sweep found two residual topical anchors of the demoted class in
`tests/test_manuscript_0512_structure.py`:

- line ~46: `assert "per-cell provenance" in body()` — the paper's own
  contribution vocabulary, an authorial term, not external terminology.
- line ~102: `assert "market dispatch" in body().lower()` — topical
  presence pin on authorial wording.

Other hits in the sweep (section headings, figure filenames, LaTeX
include paths, ORCID, backmatter section names in
`test_manuscript_frontmatter.py` and `test_abstract_numbers.py`) are
mechanical/structural and in-policy — no action.

## Relevant files

- `tests/test_manuscript_0512_structure.py` — the two anchors
- `docs/editorial-brief.md` — destination for demoted decisions
- `.claude/rules/writing.md` § CI test polarity rule — the policy

## Actions

1. For each of the two anchors, apply the 0557 triage method: if the
   underlying decision is "never state X flatly", rewrite as a negative
   guard; if it is positive editorial intent, move to
   `docs/editorial-brief.md` (entry format: **Decision:** /
   **Rationale:** / **Ticket:** / **Status:**) and delete the assertion;
   if it is genuinely structural (e.g. the term is a fixed concept the
   whole paper architecture references), document keep-in-CI in the
   brief like 0557 did for built-fleet-pipeline-tail.
2. Re-read the rest of the file while there: confirm the remaining
   assertions are mechanical (headings, labels, includes).

## Test

- Red step: rewording the per-cell-provenance sentence (same meaning,
  different words) must not fail CI after the change; before the change
  it does.

